ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362042} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ad1d3a2e-42cc-5fa0-9de5-946b7f16cdff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a stable node (sink)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362046} {:answer/id #uuid "e3512b99-f6e1-52af-b041-766c65959bba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a saddle point" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362047} {:answer/id #uuid "66657f60-2186-5401-9d4e-fd954c0b23cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "an unstable node (source)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362048}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e3512b99-f6e1-52af-b041-766c65959bba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a saddle point" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362047} :answer-field/id #uuid "5be1814d-5ca0-54e7-996c-be1bd0dc437a" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362045}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9eee4cc9-af63-536a-aed0-c7dcc751b64f" :question/math-academy-id "q-333637" :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=x(t)+3y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=3x(t)+y(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear differential equations above. The eigenvalues of the system's matrix are ${\\lambda }_{1}=4$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=-2,$ for which the corresponding eigenvectors are ${v}_{1}=[1,\\text{ }1]^{T}$ and ${v}_{2}=[-1,\\text{ }1]^{T},$ respectively. Select the correct options below regarding the given system.$\\,$\n{{field-1}} is {{field-2}} line.\n\n$\\,$\n$y=-x$ is {{field-3}} line.\n\n$\\,$\nThe equilibrium point (origin) is {{field-4}}." :question/worked-solution "The general solution of the system is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]={c}_{1}{e}^{4t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}{e}^{-2t}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\n- The line that passes through the origin and is parallel to ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ has the equation \n\n$$\ny=x.\n$$\n\nThe straight-line solutions of the form\n${c}_{1}{e}^{4t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$\nlie on that line and approach infinity as $t\\to \\infty .$ So, $y=x$ is $\\text{an unstable}$ line.\n\n- The line that passes through the origin and is parallel to ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ has the equation \n\n$$\ny=-x.\n$$\n\nThe straight-line solutions of the form\n${c}_{2}{e}^{-2t}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$\nlie on that line and approach the origin as $t\\to \\infty .$ So, $y=-x$ is $\\text{a stable}$ line.\n\nTherefore, the equilibrium point (origin) is $\\text{a saddle point}.$ \n\n**Note:** The phase portrait of the system looks as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069584/assets/a09d50fa36b2748fb1c65ed16e20d950afbbabc18884ff8718cf1571c4e13b0e.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186362049 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "35492718-d2d7-5c9d-9c02-1ef6ae0445d0" :knowledge-point/title "Classifying Systems of Linear Differential Equations With Distinct Real Eigenvalues"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "59f9777e-4b3c-50f8-a5e6-78ff3a79c58f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a stable" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362051} {:answer/id #uuid "f2a6b7e3-ff52-56d9-8c93-ce1126b6d864" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "an unstable" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362052}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f2a6b7e3-ff52-56d9-8c93-ce1126b6d864" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "an unstable" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362052} :answer-field/id #uuid "404e91c1-8a4b-529d-a64a-d5a197f1d3fb" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362050} {:ans