} :question/id #uuid "f735f61a-0791-5bf2-b5e1-a997e0f18859" :question/math-academy-id "q-333646" :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=-3x(t)-2y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=-x(t)-2y(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear differential equations above. The eigenvalues of the system's matrix are ${\\lambda }_{1}=-4$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=-1,$ for which the corresponding eigenvectors are ${v}_{1}=[2,\\text{ }1]^{T}$ and ${v}_{2}=[-1,\\text{ }1]^{T},$ respectively. Select the correct options below regarding the given system.$\\,$\n$y=\\frac{1}{2}x$ is {{field-1}} line.\n\n$\\,$\n{{field-2}} is {{field-3}} line.\n\n$\\,$\nThe equilibrium point (origin) is {{field-4}}." :question/worked-solution "The general solution of the system is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]={c}_{1}{e}^{-4t}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}{e}^{-t}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\n- The line that passes through the origin and is parallel to ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ has the equation \n\n$$\ny=\\frac{1}{2}x.\n$$\n\nThe straight-line solutions of the form\n${c}_{1}{e}^{-4t}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$\nlie on that line and approach the origin as $t\\to \\infty .$ So, $y=\\frac{1}{2}x$ is $\\text{a stable}$ line.\n\n- The line that passes through the origin and is parallel to ${v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ has the equation \n\n$$\ny=-x.\n$$\n\nThe straight-line solutions of the form\n${c}_{2}{e}^{-t}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$\nlie on that line and approach the origin as $t\\to \\infty .$ So, $y=-x$ is $\\text{a stable}$ line.\n\nTherefore, the equilibrium point (origin) is $\\text{a stable node (sink)}.$ \n\n**Note:** The phase portrait of the system looks as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069584/assets/6337a670b6fa73c4c21759b600269cb83d808a1c13026c90e2d02519fa31cd67.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186362081 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "35492718-d2d7-5c9d-9c02-1ef6ae0445d0" :knowledge-point/title "Classifying Systems of Linear Differential Equations With Distinct Real Eigenvalues"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a14b3a15-c563-5fbd-ba0e-f113b5151dda" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a stable" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362083} {:answer/id #uuid "336ef41c-4930-5152-a2e7-c97a6067f580" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "an unstable" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362084}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a14b3a15-c563-5fbd-ba0e-f113b5151dda" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a stable" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362083} :answer-field/id #uuid "3fc28926-f895-575b-baf9-b69b741af3fb" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362082} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "adc428c6-1aa0-5231-9b28-a53e2e962b51" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362086} {:answer/id #uuid "aec95aa8-0edc-55d2-a975-c4f5dc216391" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362087} {:answer/id #uuid "288b8956-75c6-52bc-bb35-11bb967b037d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362088} {:answer/id #uuid "f97ac343-b2fd-5985-a9a9-588675b609e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362089}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f97ac343-b2fd-5985-a9a9-588675b609e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362089} :answer-field/id #uuid "3c005798-0b9e-5411-8107-7b473458fa44" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362085} {:answer-field/choices [